%N A099585 Remove all 3s from prime(n) - 1.
%C A099585 a(n) equals n divided by the highest power of 3 that divides n. - _Harvey P. Dale_, Sep 29 2026
%H A099585 Harvey P. Dale, <a href="/A099585/b099585.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%t A099585 #/3^IntegerExponent[#,3]&/@(Prime[Range[70]]-1) (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Sep 29 2026 *)
%o A099585 (PARI) a(n) = (prime(n)-1)/3^valuation(prime(n)-1,3)
%Y A099585 Equals A038502( A006093(n) ). prime(n)-1 = a(n) * 3^A099584(n).
